This procedure retrieves and (optionally) rewrites sample descriptors for different media types (video, audio, text, scene) found in an MP4 sample table. The main steps are:

1. Parameter validation and lookup  
   - Verify that the sample index is in range and get the corresponding sample description box.  
2. Determine descriptor type  
   - For encrypted boxes, look up the protection scheme and pick the original data format.  
3. Switch on descriptor type  
   - For each MP4 audio, video, text, or scene subtype, check internal_type and extract the embedded ESD (Elementary Stream Descriptor).  
   - If no ESD is present for audio, fall back to creating a generic MP4A ESD when appropriate.  
   - If the subtype requires a rewrite (e.g., SVC/MVC for AVC or LHE1 for HEVC), call AVC_RewriteESDescriptorEx / HEVC_RewriteESDescriptorEx etc., passing either the sample box or NULL for inspect.  
4. Allocate and populate the output ESD  
   - For most types, allocate a new GF_ESD, fill in streamType, objectTypeIndication, and decoder‐specific data.  
   - Copy initialization parameters (audio config, video config, text config) into the new ESD.  
5. Return any error or the new ESD via *out_esd

Protection schemes (e.g. DRM) are handled by two calls into the ISOM core:  
   gf_isom_box_protector_check  
   gf_isom_box_protector_apply  

